      "title": "Identity Systems Explorer: Build One and Watch the Theorem Hold",
      "description": "An interactive single-file widget. Choose the size of the base type A, pick a basepoint a0, and slide the size of the reflexivity fibre |R(a0)|. The widget instantly reports whether the data forms a valid identity system, draws the encode/decode dictionary (a0 = a) ≃ R(a) fibre by fibre, and live-checks all three structural theorems (the fundamental equivalence, contractibility of the base fibre, and homotopy-initiality). Setting |R(a0)| to 0 or 2 demonstrates exactly how and why the identity-system conditions fail.",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n<title>Identity Systems Explorer</title>\n<style>\n  :root { --bg:#0f1226; --card:#1a1f3c; --acc:#7c5cff; --good:#3ddc97; --dim:#5a6080; --txt:#e8eaf6; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { margin:0; font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;\n         background:linear-gradient(160deg,#0b0e20,#141937); color:var(--txt); }\n  header { padding:28px 22px 10px; text-align:center; }\n  h1 { margin:0; font-size:24px; letter-spacing:.3px; }\n  p.sub { color:var(--dim); margin:6px 0 0; font-size:14px; }\n  .wrap { max-width:980px; margin:0 auto; padding:18px; display:grid; gap:18px;\n          grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }\n  .card { background:var(--card); border:1px solid #272d52; border-radius:14px;\n          padding:18px; box-shadow:0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }\n  .card.full { grid-column:1 / -1; }\n  h2 { font-size:16px; margin:0 0 10px; color:var(--acc); }\n  label { font-size:13px; color:var(--dim); display:block; margin:10px 0 4px; }\n  input[type=range]{ width:100%; }\n  .pts { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px; margin-top:8px; }\n  .pt { padding:6px 12px; border-radius:20px; border:1px solid #333a66;\n        cursor:pointer; font-size:13px; user-select:none; background:#161b38; }\n  .pt.base { background:var(--acc); border-color:var(--acc); color:#fff; font-weight:600; }\n  svg { width:100%; height:260px; }\n  .fib { font-size:13px; }\n  .tag { display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:6px; font-size:12px; }\n  .ok { background:rgba(61,220,151,.15); color:var(--good); }\n  .no { background:rgba(255,99,99,.15); color:#ff8a8a; }\n  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:13px; }\n  th,td { text-align:left; padding:6px 8px; border-bottom:1px solid #272d52; }\n  code { color:#ffd479; }\n  .big { font-size:15px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>Identity Systems Explorer</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">When does an invented relation behave exactly like equality? Build a finite identity system and watch the Fundamental Theorem hold.</p>\n</header>\n\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2>1 · Choose the base type & basepoint</h2>\n    <label>Number of points in A: <span id=\"nlab\">4</span></label>\n    <input id=\"n\" type=\"range\" min=\"2\" max=\"7\" value=\"4\" />\n    <label>Basepoint a₀ (click a point):</label>\n    <div class=\"pts\" id=\"pts\"></div>\n    <label>Fibre size over a₀ — |R(a₀)| (the reflexivity fibre):</label>\n    <input id=\"rsize\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"3\" value=\"1\" />\n    <span class=\"big\">|R(a₀)| = <code id=\"rlab\">1</code></span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2>2 · Is it an identity system?</h2>\n    <p class=\"fib\">An identity system needs the total space Σ a, R(a) to be\n       <b>contractible</b> with center <code>(a₀, rflR)</code>. For a discrete\n       base that forces <code>|R(a₀)| = 1</code> and <code>R(a) = ∅</code> for\n       a ≠ a₀ (matching the path family <code>a₀ = a</code>).</p>\n    <p class=\"big\">Status: <span id=\"status\" class=\"tag\"></span></p>\n    <p class=\"fib\" id=\"why\"></p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card full\">\n    <h2>3 · The encode/decode dictionary  (a₀ = a) ≃ R(a)</h2>\n    <svg id=\"svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 240\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card full\">\n    <h2>4 · Fibrewise table & the three theorems</h2>\n    <table id=\"tbl\">\n      <thead><tr><th>a</th><th>(a₀ = a)</th><th>R(a)</th><th>encode/decode</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody></tbody>\n    </table>\n    <p class=\"fib\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n      <b>Thm 3.3</b> encode/decode are inverse on every fibre &nbsp;\n      <span id=\"t33\" class=\"tag\"></span><br/>\n      <b>Thm 4.2</b> base fibre R(a₀) is contractible &nbsp;\n      <span id=\"t42\" class=\"tag\"></span><br/>\n      <b>Thm 4.3</b> any valid identity system here is fibrewise equivalent to the\n      path family (homotopy-initiality) &nbsp; <span id=\"t43\" class=\"tag\"></span>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\nconst state = { n:4, base:0, rsize:1 };\n\nfunction pts(){ return Array.from({length:state.n}, (_,i)=>\"a\"+i); }\n\nfunction render(){\n  // points chips\n  const P = pts();\n  const box = document.getElementById('pts'); box.innerHTML='';\n  P.forEach((p,i)=>{\n    const d=document.createElement('div');\n    d.className='pt'+(i===state.base?' base':'');\n    d.textContent=p;\n    d.onclick=()=>{ state.base=i; render(); };\n    box.appendChild(d);\n  });\n  document.getElementById('nlab').textContent=state.n;\n  document.getElementById('rlab').textContent=state.rsize;\n\n  // validity: identity system iff R(a0)=1 and R(a)=0 else (discrete)\n  const valid = state.rsize===1;\n  const st=document.getElementById('status');\n  st.textContent = valid? \"VALID identity system ✓\" : \"NOT an identity system ✗\";\n  st.className = \"tag \"+(valid?\"ok\":\"no\");\n  document.getElementById('why').textContent = valid\n    ? \"Total space = {(a₀, rflR)} is a single point = its own center. R behaves exactly like the path family.\"\n    : (state.rsize===0\n        ? \"R(a₀) is empty: there is no reflexivity witness, so the center (a₀, rflR) does not exist.\"\n        : \"R(a₀) has \"+state.rsize+\" elements: the total space has \"+state.rsize+\" points and cannot collapse to a single center.\");\n\n  // svg dictionary\n  const svg=document.getElementById('svg'); svg.innerHTML='';\n  const NS=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n  const rowH=200/Math.max(P.length,1);\n  P.forEach((a,i)=>{\n    const y=20+rowH*i+rowH/2;\n    const isBase = i===state.base;\n    const pathCard = isBase ? \"{ rfl }\" : \"∅\";\n    const rCard = isBase ? (state.rsize===1?\"{ rflR }\":(state.rsize===0?\"∅\":\"{\"+state.rsize+\" elts}\")) : \"∅\";\n    const ok = isBase ? (state.rsize===1) : true;\n    const col = ok? \"#3ddc97\" : \"#ff8a8a\";\n    const txt=(x,t,anchor)=>{const e=document.createElementNS(NS,'text');\n      e.setAttribute('x',x);e.setAttribute('y',y+4);e.setAttribute('fill','#e8eaf6');\n      e.setAttribute('font-size','15');e.setAttribute('text-anchor',anchor);e.textContent=t;svg.appendChild(e);};\n    txt(60,\"(a₀=\"+a+\") = \"+pathCard,'start');\n    txt(840,\"R(\"+a+\") = \"+rCard,'end');\n    const line=document.createElementNS(NS,'line');\n    line.setAttribute('x1',360);line.setAttribute('y1',y);\n    line.setAttribute('x2',540);line.setAttribute('y2',y);\n    line.setAttribute('stroke',col);line.setAttribute('stroke-width',ok?3:1.5);\n    if(!ok) line.setAttribute('stroke-dasharray','5,5');\n    svg.appendChild(line);\n    [[360,'start'],[540,'end']].forEach(([x])=>{const c=document.createElementNS(NS,'circle');\n      c.setAttribute('cx',x);c.setAttribute('cy',y);c.setAttribute('r',4);c.setAttribute('fill',col);svg.appendChild(c);});\n    const lab=document.createElementNS(NS,'text');lab.setAttribute('x',450);lab.setAttribute('y',y-8);\n    lab.setAttribute('fill',col);lab.setAttribute('font-size','11');lab.setAttribute('text-anchor','middle');\n    lab.textContent= ok? \"≃\" : \"≄\"; svg.appendChild(lab);\n  });\n\n  // table + theorems\n  const tb=document.querySelector('#tbl tbody'); tb.innerHTML='';\n  let t33=true;\n  P.forEach((a,i)=>{\n    const isBase=i===state.base;\n    const lp= isBase?1:0;\n    const lr= isBase?state.rsize:0;\n    const ok= lp===lr;\n    t33 = t33 && ok;\n    const tr=document.createElement('tr');\n    tr.innerHTML=`<td>${a}</td><td>${lp}</td><td>${lr}</td>`+\n      `<td><span class=\"tag ${ok?'ok':'no'}\">${ok?'bijection':'mismatch'}</span></td>`;\n    tb.appendChild(tr);\n  });\n  const set=(id,b)=>{const e=document.getElementById(id);e.textContent=b?'holds ✓':'fails ✗';e.className='tag '+(b?'ok':'no');};\n  set('t33', t33 && valid);\n  set('t42', valid);\n  set('t43', valid);\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById('n').oninput=e=>{state.n=+e.target.value; if(state.base>=state.n)state.base=0; render();};\ndocument.getElementById('rsize').oninput=e=>{state.rsize=+e.target.value; render();};\nrender();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    }
